  <section>
    <h2>2. PRELIMINARIES</h2>
    <h3>Definition 2.1.</h3>
    <p>Catalan's triangle is the array <span data-field="C_n_k_array">{{ C_n_k_array }}</span>, where <span data-field="k_range_def21">{{ k_range_def21 }}</span>, defined by <span data-field="C_n_k_formula">{{ C_n_k_formula }}</span> for all <span data-field="n_range_def21">{{ n_range_def21 }}</span>, <span data-field="C_n_k_recurrence">{{ C_n_k_recurrence }}</span> for <span data-field="n_range_def22">{{ n_range_def22 }}</span>, and <span data-field="C_n_n_formula">{{ C_n_n_formula }}</span>.</p>
    <p>Below we show rows zero through four of Catalan's triangle.</p>
    <table>
      <tr>
        <td>1</td>
